If you have explicitly set your module kind to be plain , Kotlin creates an object that contains all Kotlin declarations from the current module. This is done to prevent spoiling the global object. This means that for a module myModule , all declarations are available to JavaScript via the myModule object. For example:

fun foo() = "Hello"

This function can be called from JavaScript like this:

alert(myModule.foo());

Calling the function directly like this is not applicable when you compile your Kotlin module to JavaScript modules like UMD (the default setting for both browser and nodejs targets), ESM , CommonJS , or AMD . In these cases, your declarations are exposed according to the chosen JavaScript module system. For example, when using UMD, ESM, or CommonJS, your call site would look like this:

alert(require('myModule').foo());","title":"Use Kotlin code from JavaScript","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-to-kotlin-interop.html","sections":["Use Kotlin code from JavaScript > Isolating declarations in a separate JavaScript object in plain mode"],"line_start":5,"line_end":17,"score":0.6229556202888489,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"declare-parameters-with-default-values","start":3296,"end":3902,"split_code":false,"platforms":["js"],"id":"712359572c81b236f5c6335f575dd71d78b687a5a7fae28ff9f33488260e6d33","document_id":"js-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"Declare parameters with default values

If you are writing an external declaration for a JavaScript function which has a parameter with a default value, use definedExternally . This delegates the generation of the default values to the JavaScript function itself:

external fun myFunWithOptionalArgs(
    x: Int,
    y: String = definedExternally,
    z: String = definedExternally
)

With this external declaration, you can call myFunWithOptionalArgs with one required argument and two optional arguments, where the default values are calculated by the JavaScript implementation of myFunWithOptionalArgs .","title":"Use JavaScript code from Kotlin","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-interop.html","sections":["Use JavaScript code from Kotlin > external modifier > Declare parameters with default values"],"line_start":87,"line_end":97,"score":0.6221352815628052,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"javascript-properties","start":1209,"end":1507,"split_code":false,"platforms":["wasm"],"id":"a3dffcb2f626ca1873e07f1b0e5a76cd022d71657f175b21a38b508b27a723e2","document_id":"wasm-js-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"JavaScript properties

