Kotlin was first designed for easy interoperation with the Java platform: it sees Java classes as Kotlin classes, and Java sees Kotlin classes as Java classes.

However, JavaScript is a dynamically typed language, which means it does not check types at compile time. You can freely talk to JavaScript from Kotlin via dynamic types. If you want to use the full power of the Kotlin type system, you can create external declarations for JavaScript libraries which will be understood by the Kotlin compiler and the surrounding tooling.","title":"Use JavaScript code from Kotlin","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-interop.html","sections":["Use JavaScript code from Kotlin"],"line_start":1,"line_end":5,"score":0.6442992687225342,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"declare-static-members-of-a-class","start":2600,"end":3294,"split_code":false,"platforms":["js"],"id":"060b1716cf02e76f9cf790cff97af5e52be67ec32a4a2ead8cf56a9c78ab2117","document_id":"js-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"Declare (static) members of a class

In JavaScript, you can define members either on a prototype or a class itself:

function MyClass() { ... }
MyClass.sharedMember = function() { /* implementation */ };
MyClass.prototype.ownMember = function() { /* implementation */ };

There is no such syntax in Kotlin. However, in Kotlin we have companion objects. Kotlin treats companion objects of external classes in a special way: instead of expecting an object, it assumes members of companion objects to be members of the class itself. MyClass from the example above can be described as follows:

external class MyClass {
    companion object {
        fun sharedMember()
    }

    fun ownMember()
}","title":"Use JavaScript code from Kotlin","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-interop.html","sections":["Use JavaScript code from Kotlin > external modifier > Declare (static) members of a class"],"line_start":69,"line_end":85,"score":0.6020947694778442,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"external-interfaces","start":2008,"end":2612,"split_code":false,"platforms":["wasm"],"id":"6ef84fc36bcda64a15353bd9bda36bf7eae59bdef82b47d47a7e663a56cffb33","document_id":"wasm-js-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"External interfaces

